{"id": "EUVD-2026-91476", "enisaUuid": "ba44062e-9246-3bca-aa1e-a4538aa4f150", "description": "YesWiki before 4.6.7 contains a reflected cross-site scripting vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to inject scripts via the field parameter of the mail handler. Attackers can craft links whose field value breaks out of the ajax-mail-form action attribute to execute JavaScript in victims' browsers.", "datePublished": "2026-10-02T11:38:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-06T16:19:13", "baseScore": 5.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/YesWiki/yeswiki/security/advisories/GHSA-2fc6-rvp3-fgfj", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/yeswiki-before-4.6.7-reflected-xss-via-field-parameter-in-mail-handler"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-104465", "GHSA-m338-cjqw-rxwv"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d8675201-2ffc-334a-814f-e97773c308d9", "product": {"name": "yeswiki", "vendor": {"name": "YesWiki"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.6.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "08a10398-d724-3650-bc4f-ff0163643c7c", "vendor": {"name": "YesWiki"}}], "isExploited": false}